  "frame-multiplexer": {
    "solutionCode": "#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct FrameChunk {\n    pub stream_id: u8,\n    pub offset: u32,\n    pub payload: String,\n    pub is_last: bool,\n}\n\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub struct StreamResult {\n    pub stream_id: u8,\n    pub data: String,\n    pub complete: bool,\n}\n\npub struct Solution;\n\nimpl Solution {\n    pub fn reassemble_streams(chunks: Vec<FrameChunk>) -> Vec<StreamResult> {\n        use std::collections::BTreeMap;\n\n        let mut streams: BTreeMap<u8, (Vec<FrameChunk>, Option<u32>)> = BTreeMap::new();\n        for chunk in chunks {\n            let entry = streams.entry(chunk.stream_id).or_insert_with(|| (Vec::new(), None));\n            if chunk.is_last {\n                let end_offset = chunk.offset + chunk.payload.len() as u32;\n                entry.1 = Some(entry.1.map_or(end_offset, |curr| curr.max(end_offset)));\n            }\n            entry.0.push(chunk);\n        }\n\n        let mut results = Vec::with_capacity(streams.len());\n\n        for (stream_id, (mut stream_chunks, expected_total_len)) in streams {\n            stream_chunks.sort_unstable_by(|a, b| {\n                a.offset.cmp(&b.offset).then_with(|| b.payload.len().cmp(&a.payload.len()))\n            });\n\n            let mut assembled = match expected_total_len {\n                Some(len) => Vec::with_capacity(len as usize),\n                None => Vec::new(),\n            };\n            let mut current_offset: u32 = 0;\n\n            for chunk in stream_chunks {\n                let chunk_start = chunk.offset;\n                let chunk_bytes = chunk.payload.as_bytes();\n                let chunk_len = chunk_bytes.len() as u32;\n                let chunk_end = chunk_start + chunk_len;\n\n                if chunk_end <= current_offset {\n                    continue;\n                }\n\n                if chunk_start > current_offset {\n                    break;\n                }\n\n                let slice_start = (current_offset - chunk_start) as usize;\n                assembled.extend_from_slice(&chunk_bytes[slice_start..]);\n                current_offset = chunk_end;\n            }\n\n            let complete = match expected_total_len {\n                Some(total) => current_offset == total,\n                None => false,\n            };\n\n            let data = String::from_utf8(assembled).unwrap_or_default();\n\n            results.push(StreamResult {\n                stream_id,\n                data,\n                complete,\n            });\n        }\n\n        results\n    }\n}",
    "solutionWalkthrough": "Group arriving frames by `stream_id` using a `BTreeMap` to naturally produce streams in sorted order. For each stream, track whether a terminal (`is_last`) frame was received and its expected total length. Sort frames by `offset` ascending, then merge contiguous byte slices into a buffer while seamlessly skipping duplicate or overlapping sub-slices. If an offset gap is encountered before reaching the next frame, terminate contiguous assembly early. Finally, verify if the assembled byte length matches the terminal offset to assert stream completeness."
  },
